# Boss_Harley_StepPole: the 130 px cap ($01A1EC), Harley killed near the top of a pole rise
# (ruling 5, 2), at its first call (the Harley boss: a6 its object, $10(a6) the pole block). The
# state: the death script's Boss_Harley_SetPoleTarget ($019A10: target $3C, acceleration $1800,
# negated because the pole is above $3C) came while the pole still rose fast toward $78 (velocity
# not reset), and nine frames of coasting later it passes 130 px. A real state: the TAS's rise
# from $46 to $78 (TAS f5783-5822, the pole block $FFC488) is ~40 frames long and the TAS lands
# hits on Harley during it (g_BossEnergy $0370 -> $02F0); a final hit in its frames 5818-5822
# (any later rise of the pattern loop at $019538 too) leaves the pole at height $0081F41E with
# velocity $000174C9 after nine death frames (from 5820's dump, stepped as the asm does: scratchpad
# cov13_polesim.py), so the next step gives 131.3 px and the cap. The TAS's own last hit came
# during a descent (f5966); the corpus never killed Harley in that window.

case killed_rising
l {a6 + $10} = $003C0000
l {a6 + $10} + 4 = $0081F41E
l {a6 + $10} + 8 = $000174C9
l {a6 + $10} + $C = $FFFFE800
